---
title: Capture Records
sidebar:
  label: Capture records
  order: 4
---

Capture records connect a specimen to the collecting event, site, coordinate,
method, and collector that produced it.

{% steps %}

1. Choose the `Site ID`. The `Event ID` list then shows only that site's
   collecting events.
2. Choose the `Event ID`.
3. Fill in the capture details below.

{% /steps %}

Changing the site or the event asks for confirmation, then clears this card
except the capture date and time. When you change only the event, the
coordinate is kept if it belongs to the same site.

| Field | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| `Capture date`, `Capture time` | When the specimen was captured. |
| `Relative time` | Replaces the exact time with `Dawn`, `Morning`, `Afternoon`, `Dusk`, or `Night`. Shown after `Show more`. |
| `Method` | A collection method from the selected event. |
| `Method ID` | Optional trap, net, or other method identifier. Shown after `Show more`. |
| `Coordinate ID` | A coordinate of the event's site. |
| `Coordinate extent (m)` | Optional positive distance the capture extends beyond the coordinate point. |
| `Collector` | Optional, from the event's personnel. Shown when it has a value, after `Show more`, or always if `Always show collector field` is on in Settings. |

In Darwin Core exports, a positive coordinate extent is added to the saved
coordinate uncertainty. If the coordinate has no valid uncertainty, the extent
is used by itself. Empty, zero, and negative values are ignored.
